# How to cite this software, read by GitHub ("Cite this repository"). Zenodo uses .zenodo.json
# instead whenever it exists; keep both in step, and this version with pyproject.toml.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below, and cite AHAH itself: Daras et al. 2019, doi:10.1038/s41597-019-0114-6."
title: "datazone-ahah: AHAH for SQL Server"
abstract: >-
  A CLI pipeline that puts every edition of the Access to Healthy Assets and Hazards index
  (AHAH, versions 1 to 5.1) for Scottish data zones into one SQL Server table, values exactly as
  published, from hash-pinned sources, with a row digest that a load is checked against.
authors:
  - family-names: Tinti
    given-names: Michele
    affiliation: "Health Informatics Centre (HIC), University of Dundee"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0051-017X"
version: "0.1.0"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23783415"   # the concept DOI: every release; each release also has its own
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/mtinti/datazone-ahah"
keywords:
  - AHAH
  - Access to Healthy Assets and Hazards
  - data zone
  - SQL Server
  - data linkage
  - Scotland
